<section class="section-soft">
<div class="wrap split">
<div class="prose reveal">
<h2 class="h2">Consistency parents can plan around.</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>For families, the value isn't a one-off ride — it's the same vetted chauffeur, the same standard, the same arrival window, every day. A consistent primary chauffeur, with any approved backup communicated in advance — never an unannounced substitute. Routes and schedules are set in advance with the parents or family office, and changes go to one accountable contact.</p>
<p>Tell us the ages and number of children when you set up the route and the correct seating is arranged. Discretion and a calm, professional presence are part of the standard.</p>
</div>
<div class="figure reveal">
<div class="kicker">Same<br>route.<br><em>Same hands.</em></div>
<p>Set up by the week or term. Coordinated directly with parents or the family office — never improvised day to day.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section-dark">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="grid-head reveal" style="margin-bottom:28px">
<p class="eyebrow on-dark">Setting Up a Family Route</p>
<h2 class="h2">What we confirm before the first pickup.</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
</div>
<div class="faq reveal">
<details><summary>What if the primary chauffeur is unavailable one day?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">An approved backup chauffeur, known to the family in advance, covers the route — never an unannounced substitute showing up cold.</div></details>
<details><summary>Who is authorized to change pickup times or details?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Only the parents, guardians, or family office contacts named when the route is set up. Changes from anyone else are confirmed with an authorized contact before they're made.</div></details>
<details><summary>What information do you need about the child?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Age, height, and weight, to arrange the correct child seat or booster — plus an emergency contact on file separate from the day-to-day authorized contacts.</div></details>
<details><summary>How is drop-off confirmed?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">The chauffeur confirms arrival at school and a completed handoff — the child is not left at a drop point unconfirmed.</div></details>
<details><summary>Can I set this up weekly, monthly, or for the school term?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes — routes are typically arranged by the week, month, or full term, whichever matches the family's schedule.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the cancellation policy for a single day?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Tell your authorized contact as early as possible; standing routes are held for the arranged schedule, and single-day changes are handled directly, not through a general cancellation form.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is our information kept private?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes — route details, schedules, and any information about the children are shared only with the assigned chauffeur and are not discussed outside the arrangement.</div></details>
</div>
</div>
